7. BOARD RENDERING

- The chessboard is rendered on a square Canvas.
- Three themes: light (default), dark, and contrast (high-contrast for color-blind users), plus auto to match system theme.
- Additional board color schemes: blue/black, green/black, brown/cream, tournament (green/white).
- Pieces use standard Unicode chess glyphs by default; an alternate SVG piece set is available in settings.
- Highlight states:
  - Selected square — highlighted when the user taps a piece.
  - Legal move indicators — small dots on legal destination squares.
  - Last move — both source and destination squares highlighted with a subtle overlay.
  - Check — the checked king's square tinted red.
  - Best move arrow — rendered over the board in all modes when analysis is available.
  - Threat arrow — optional secondary arrow showing the opponent's best threat (toggleable).
- Coordinates — displayed on the edges of the board (a–h, 1–8), toggleable.
- Haptic feedback — light vibration on move classification (blunder = strong buzz, best move = gentle tap), toggleable.

