10. ONBOARDING

10.1 First-Launch Screens

Three intro screens, each with a single illustration and one line of text:

1. "Analyze any chess position — study games, review moves, solve puzzles."
2. "Load a PGN, share a screenshot, or use the live overlay."
3. "All analysis happens on your phone. Nothing is uploaded."

10.2 Ethics Disclaimer

After the intro screens, a mandatory ethics screen appears:

> "Chess Forge is a training and analysis tool for studying positions, reviewing games, and solving puzzles. Using it in live online chess games violates the terms of service of most chess platforms and may result in account bans. Chess Forge is not intended for, and its developers do not condone, use in live competitive play."

A single "I Understand" button dismisses the screen. The user must tap it to proceed. This screen also appears after every app update if the ethics text has changed.

10.3 Permissions Walkthrough

The onboarding flow ends with a permissions walkthrough:
- Screen A: "To use live overlay, Chess Forge needs to see your screen." → Button opens MediaProjection dialog.
- Screen B: "To draw arrows on top of your chess app, Chess Forge needs to draw over other apps." → Button opens SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW settings.

Each permission screen can be skipped. The user can grant permissions later from Settings → Overlay.

