11. DATA MODEL

The app stores the following locally (Room database + SharedPreferences):

- Analysis history — every FEN analyzed with its result, timestamp, source mode, move classification, and session grouping.
- Game records — reconstructed games from overlay sessions and loaded PGNs, with move classifications and accuracy data.
- Puzzle database — generated puzzles with ratings, solution lines, and source references.
- Puzzle progress — user's puzzle rating, solved/attempted history, statistics by category.
- User settings — engine preset, classification thresholds, board theme, appearance, overlay preferences, active profile.
- Profiles — named setting combinations.
- Board region — the saved rectangle for Screenshot and Overlay modes.
- Onboarding state — which intro screens have been seen, ethics disclaimer version.
- Backups — locally stored `.forgebackup` files (if auto-backup is enabled).

No user account, no cloud sync, no server communication (except opt-in crash reports).

---

12. ERROR HANDLING

The app must fail gracefully in all of the following scenarios:

- Stockfish fails to start — show "Engine error — please restart the app"; retry up to 3 times. If the deep instance fails, fall back to a single-instance mode with a notification.
- YOLO model fails to load — show "Vision model error — please reinstall"; block Screenshot, Overlay, and Puzzle modes; Practice Mode still works.
- Board not detected in screenshot — show "Could not find a board in this image"; allow retry or manual crop.
- Confidence below 0.75 — show confidence-specific message; allow retry.
- FEN validation fails — show which squares failed validation; allow manual correction by tapping squares to cycle through piece options.
- MediaProjection dies mid-capture (Overlay) — show "Screen capture was interrupted"; prompt to re-grant permission.
- SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW revoked mid-session (Overlay) — stop the overlay; show "Overlay permission was revoked."
- Device rotated during overlay — pause capture; show "Please rotate back to resume."
- Screen locked — pause capture; resume automatically on unlock.
- Device runs out of memory — cancel deep analysis first, then quick analysis if needed; show "Not enough memory — try a lower depth."
- User force-stops the app — all services terminate cleanly; no zombie notifications.
- Corrupted backup file — show "Backup file is corrupted or incompatible"; do not partially import.
- Puzzle generation fails — show "Could not generate a puzzle from this position"; the position is still available for normal analysis.

