14. ACCESSIBILITY

- TalkBack support — all UI elements have content descriptions. The board is navigable via swipe gestures with spoken square names ("e4, white pawn").
- Color-blind mode — arrows use patterns (striped, dotted, solid) in addition to colors. Evaluation bar uses shapes (▲▼) in addition to color. Board uses the high-contrast theme.
- Font scaling — all text respects system font size.
- High contrast mode — increases arrow outline width, evaluation badge contrast, and board square contrast.
- Reduced motion — disables pulse animation, arrow fade effects, and shake animations.
- One-handed mode — moves primary controls to the bottom of the screen for large devices.
- Screen reader optimized — puzzle mode provides audio hints ("The knight on f3 can jump to e5").

